Dear Daniel,

Thank you for your message and for sharing your proposal. I had a
look, and before we set up a meeting I would like to understand more
clearly how this line of work would deepen our understanding of real
estate investments at the asset or cross-sectional level. In
particular, I am interested in how your approach would speak to the
specific frictions and characteristics of the real estate asset class,
rather than primarily time-series dynamics.

If you can elaborate briefly on this connection, I will be better able
to assess how well the project fits with my supervision interests and
the department=E2=80=99s focus. I do take on new PhD students when there is=
 a
strong alignment, so I am open to continuing the conversation once I
have a clearer sense of the real estate angle.

Best regards,
Thies

